@.str.21 = private unnamed_addr constant [3823 x i8] c"\0A\0A# Examples\0A\0A* Show one path through the dependency graph leading from Hello to\0A  Glibc:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix why-depends nixpkgs#hello nixpkgs#glibc\0A  /nix/store/v5sv61sszx301i0x6xysaqzla09nksnd-hello-2.10\0A  \E2\94\94\E2\94\80\E2\94\80\E2\94\80bin/hello: \E2\80\A6...................../nix/store/9l06v7fc38c1x3r2iydl15ksgz0ysb82-glibc-2.32/lib/ld-linux-x86-64.\E2\80\A6\0A      \E2\86\92 /nix/store/9l06v7fc38c1x3r2iydl15ksgz0ysb82-glibc-2.32\0A  ```\0A\0A* Show all files and paths in the dependency graph leading from\0A  Thunderbird to libX11:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix why-depends --all nixpkgs#thunderbird nixpkgs#xorg.libX11\0A  /nix/store/qfc8729nzpdln1h0hvi1ziclsl3m84sr-thunderbird-78.5.1\0A  \E2\94\9C\E2\94\80\E2\94\80\E2\94\80lib/thunderbird/libxul.so: \E2\80\A66wrw-libxcb-1.14/lib:/nix/store/adzfjjh8w25vdr0xdx9x16ah4f5rqrw5-libX11-1.7.0/lib:/nix/store/ssf\E2\80\A6\0A  \E2\94\82   \E2\86\92 /nix/store/adzfjjh8w25vdr0xdx9x16ah4f5rqrw5-libX11-1.7.0\0A  \E2\94\9C\E2\94\80\E2\94\80\E2\94\80lib/thunderbird/libxul.so: \E2\80\A6pxyc-libXt-1.2.0/lib:/nix/store/1qj29ipxl2fyi2b13l39hdircq17gnk0-libXdamage-1.1.5/lib:/nix/store\E2\80\A6\0A  \E2\94\82   \E2\86\92 /nix/store/1qj29ipxl2fyi2b13l39hdircq17gnk0-libXdamage-1.1.5\0A  \E2\94\82   \E2\94\9C\E2\94\80\E2\94\80\E2\94\80lib/libXdamage.so.1.1.0: \E2\80\A6-libXfixes-5.0.3/lib:/nix/store/adzfjjh8w25vdr0xdx9x16ah4f5rqrw5-libX11-1.7.0/lib:/nix/store/9l0\E2\80\A6\0A  \E2\94\82   \E2\94\82   \E2\86\92 /nix/store/adzfjjh8w25vdr0xdx9x16ah4f5rqrw5-libX11-1.7.0\0A  \E2\80\A6\0A  ```\0A\0A* Show why Glibc depends on itself:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix why-depends nixpkgs#glibc nixpkgs#glibc\0A  /nix/store/9df65igwjmf2wbw0gbrrgair6piqjgmi-glibc-2.31\0A  \E2\94\94\E2\94\80\E2\94\80\E2\94\80lib/ld-2.31.so: \E2\80\A6che       Do not use /nix/store/9df65igwjmf2wbw0gbrrgair6piqjgmi-glibc-2.31/etc/ld.so.cache.  --\E2\80\A6\0A      \E2\86\92 /nix/store/9df65igwjmf2wbw0gbrrgair6piqjgmi-glibc-2.31\0A  ```\0A\0A* Show why Geeqie has a build-time dependency on `systemd`:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix why-depends --derivation nixpkgs#geeqie nixpkgs#systemd\0A  /nix/store/drrpq2fqlrbj98bmazrnww7hm1in3wgj-geeqie-1.4.drv\0A  \E2\94\94\E2\94\80\E2\94\80\E2\94\80/: \E2\80\A6atch.drv\22,[\22out\22]),(\22/nix/store/qzh8dyq3lfbk3i1acbp7x9wh3il2imiv-gtk+3-3.24.21.drv\22,[\22dev\22]),(\22/\E2\80\A6\0A      \E2\86\92 /nix/store/qzh8dyq3lfbk3i1acbp7x9wh3il2imiv-gtk+3-3.24.21.drv\0A      \E2\94\94\E2\94\80\E2\94\80\E2\94\80/: \E2\80\A616.0.drv\22,[\22dev\22]),(\22/nix/store/8kp79fyslf3z4m3dpvlh6w46iaadz5c2-cups-2.3.3.drv\22,[\22dev\22]),(\22/nix\E2\80\A6\0A          \E2\86\92 /nix/store/8kp79fyslf3z4m3dpvlh6w46iaadz5c2-cups-2.3.3.drv\0A          \E2\94\94\E2\94\80\E2\94\80\E2\94\80/: \E2\80\A6.3.1.drv\22,[\22out\22]),(\22/nix/store/yd3ihapyi5wbz1kjacq9dbkaq5v5hqjg-systemd-246.4.drv\22,[\22dev\22]),(\22/\E2\80\A6\0A              \E2\86\92 /nix/store/yd3ihapyi5wbz1kjacq9dbkaq5v5hqjg-systemd-246.4.drv\0A  ```\0A\0A# Description\0A\0ANix automatically determines potential runtime dependencies between\0Astore paths by scanning for the *hash parts* of store paths. For\0Ainstance, if there exists a store path\0A`/nix/store/9df65igwjmf2wbw0gbrrgair6piqjgmi-glibc-2.31`, and a file\0Ainside another store path contains the string `9df65igw\E2\80\A6`, then the\0Alatter store path *refers* to the former, and thus might need it at\0Aruntime. Nix always maintains the existence of the transitive closure\0Aof a store path under the references relationship; it is therefore not\0Apossible to install a store path without having all of its references\0Apresent.\0A\0ASometimes Nix packages end up with unexpected runtime dependencies;\0Afor instance, a reference to a compiler might accidentally end up in a\0Abinary, causing the former to be in the latter's closure. This kind of\0A*closure size bloat* is undesirable.\0A\0A`nix why-depends` allows you to diagnose the cause of such issues. It\0Ashows why the store path *package* depends on the store path\0A*dependency*, by showing a shortest sequence in the references graph\0Afrom the former to the latter. Also, for each node along this path, it\0Ashows a file fragment containing a reference to the next store path in\0Athe sequence.\0A\0ATo show why derivation *package* has a build-time rather than runtime\0Adependency on derivation *dependency*, use `--derivation`.\0A\0A\00", align 1
